# UX SOVEREIGNTY: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

> **Mandate**: Consolidates `ux_lead.mdc` + `ui_ux_mastery.mdc`. One rule, absolute authority. All UIs must adhere to the Liquid Glass aesthetic and rigorous accessibility standards.

## 1. LIQUID GLASS AESTHETIC (Tailwind & Framer Motion)
```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED: Standard Liquid Glass Card with Framer Motion hover physics
import { motion } from 'framer-motion';

export const GlassCard = ({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) => (
  <motion.div
    whileHover={{ y: -4, scale: 1.01 }}
    whileTap={{ scale: 0.98 }}
    transition={{ type: "spring", stiffness: 300, damping: 20 }}
    className="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/40 backdrop-blur-xl shadow-2xl p-6"
  >
    {/* Subtle gradient overlay for specular highlight */}
    <div className="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-white/5 to-transparent pointer-events-none" />
    <div className="relative z-10">{children}</div>
  </motion.div>
);
```

## 2. STAGGERED LIST ANIMATIONS
```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED: Use variants for staggered list rendering
const container = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0 },
  show: {
    opacity: 1,
    transition: { staggerChildren: 0.1, delayChildren: 0.2 }
  }
};

const item = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 20 },
  show: { opacity: 1, y: 0, transition: { type: "spring" } }
};

// Usage: <motion.ul variants={container} initial="hidden" animate="show">
